#
# Semantic content of <monetary.h> beyond the names the Tier 0 header check
# covers: the types and declarations the page gives, checked at build time.
# The header mutants for these arrive with the Tier 0 generator, so each
# says why it has no mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.monetary.h.001
anchor     basedefs/monetary.h.html#DESCRIPTION/locale_t
class      required
says       <monetary.h> alone defines the type locale_t.
test       t/001-types-locale.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.monetary.h.002
anchor     basedefs/monetary.h.html#DESCRIPTION/size_t
class      required
says       <monetary.h> alone defines size_t as an unsigned integer type.
note       The page defers to <stddef.h>.
test       t/002-types-size.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.monetary.h.003
anchor     basedefs/monetary.h.html#DESCRIPTION/ssize_t
class      required
says       <monetary.h> alone defines ssize_t as a signed integer type.
note       The page defers to <sys/types.h>.
test       t/003-types-ssize.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.monetary.h.004
anchor     basedefs/monetary.h.html#DESCRIPTION/strfmon
class      required
says       <monetary.h> declares strfmon() and strfmon_l() as variadic
           functions with the prototypes the page gives (a function without a
           prototype, or with other parameter or result types, does not
           match).
test       t/004-functions.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
